Industrial Internship Report
Crop and Weed Detection using YOLOv8 & Turbofan Engine Remaining Useful Life Prediction
Prepared by

Jnanesh M

Domain: Machine Learning / Data Science

upSkill Campus | The IoT Academy | UniConverge Technologies Pvt. Ltd. (UCT)
Executive Summary

This report presents the work completed during the Industrial Internship provided by upSkill Campus and The IoT Academy in collaboration with UniConverge Technologies Pvt. Ltd. (UCT). Two Machine Learning projects were completed: Crop and Weed Detection using YOLOv8, and Turbofan Engine Remaining Useful Life prediction using the NASA C-MAPSS FD001 dataset. The internship provided practical exposure to dataset preparation, model training, evaluation, GitHub documentation, and industry-style reporting.
1 Preface
This report summarizes the complete internship work. A relevant internship helps connect academic learning with industry-style problem solving, deadlines, and documentation.
The first project detects crops and weeds from field images using object detection. The second project estimates remaining useful life of turbofan engines from sensor data, which is useful for predictive maintenance.
upSkill Campus and UCT provided weekly learning material, project problem statements, quizzes, and a final GitHub submission process. I thank the mentors and management team of upSkill Campus, The IoT Academy, and UniConverge Technologies Pvt. Ltd. for this opportunity.
Message to juniors: start the project early, keep GitHub organized from day one, and write the report while doing the project.
