2.6 Glossary

YOLO: You Only Look Once, object detection algorithm
YOLOv8: Ultralytics object detection model
RUL: Remaining Useful Life
C-MAPSS: Commercial Modular Aero-Propulsion System Simulation
RMSE / MAE / R²: regression evaluation metrics
mAP: Mean Average Precision
UCT / USC: UniConverge Technologies / upSkill Campus

3 Problem Statement
Project 1: Crop and Weed Detection

Weeds compete with crops for nutrients, water, and sunlight. Manual identification is slow. The task was to detect and classify crop and weed regions in field images using bounding boxes.
Project 2: Turbofan Engine RUL Prediction

Machines degrade over time. If failure is not predicted early, downtime increases. The task was to predict Remaining Useful Life of turbofan engines using NASA C-MAPSS FD001 sensor data.
4 Existing and Proposed Solution
Existing crop-weed methods include manual inspection and simple image processing. These are less robust in real field conditions. The proposed solution uses YOLOv8 transfer learning with an organized train/validation dataset.
Existing RUL methods include scheduled maintenance and simple threshold alerts. The proposed solution uses RUL labeling, removal of constant sensors, scaling, and comparison of Random Forest, Gradient Boosting, and XGBoost.
