5 Proposed Design / Model
5.1 Crop and Weed Detection flow
Input images → separate images and labels → train/val split → data.yaml → train YOLOv8n → evaluate → save weights and prediction results.
5.2 Turbofan RUL flow
Load FD001 files → name columns → calculate RUL → drop constant sensors → scale features → train models → compare RMSE, MAE, R² → save best model and plot.
5.3 Interfaces
Project 1: Colab/Jupyter + Ultralytics YOLO + data.yaml. Inference is on images, not live camera.

Project 2: Colab/Jupyter + Pandas, Scikit-learn, XGBoost, Matplotlib, joblib.
6 Performance Test
6.1 Test Plan

Crop-Weed: check folder structure, data.yaml, training completion, sample inference
RUL: check dataset loading, RUL calculation, metrics, saved model and plot

6.2 Test Procedure
YOLOv8n was trained on Google Colab GPU. Path issues between local system and Drive were fixed through data.yaml. RUL models were trained on processed FD001 features and compared using regression metrics.
6.3 Performance Outcome
Crop-Weed training completed and produced evaluation visuals and saved weights. Main constraints were Colab GPU limits and file-path errors.
RUL models were compared using RMSE, MAE, and R². The best model and prediction plot were saved. Main constraints were constant-sensor removal and Colab path setup.
7 My Learnings
I learned YOLO dataset setup, object detection training, RUL labeling, preprocessing, model comparison, evaluation metrics, GitHub organization, and professional reporting. These skills will help in future internships, MCA project work, and AI/ML applications.
